+// Persistent layer tail for 1..8 token rows (exl3_tail_m16_kernel.cuh, ext 8202): the attention/GDN
+// output projection (6144 -> 5120, 4 bpw mul1), the attention residual add, the post-attention
+// RMSNorm and ext 8201's fused MLP (5120 -> 17408 -> 5120, SiLU) in one cooperative launch, following
+// the Bend-emitted schedules exl3_tail_m16_sched.h and exl3_mlp_m16_sched.h. Supported: those shapes,
+// 4 bpw mul1 trellises, m 1..8, and a grid of exactly the schedule's G blocks (2 per SM) on the
+// current device. EXL3_LAYER_TAIL=0 disables it (callers keep the separate o_proj / norm / MLP).
+
+// L2 prefetch depth across the o_proj -> gate/up transition (phase-1 tiles per warp past the ring):
+// returns the value used by later launches; set >= 0 changes it (benchmark knob, default
+// EXL3_TAIL_M16_L2PF or 0). The down-phase prefetch keeps 8201's knob (exl3_mlp_m16_l2pf).
+int exl3_tail_m16_l2pf(int set);
+
+bool exl3_tail_m16_supported
